Gnumeric 1.12.62 and GOffice 0.10.62

The native runtime archive was built from the unmodified official releases.
Both products offer a choice of GPL version 2 or GPL version 3. LICENSE contains
the complete GPL version 2 and LICENSES/gpl-3.0.txt contains GPL version 3.
LICENSES/gnumeric.txt and LICENSES/goffice.txt preserve the upstream dual-license
notices; their COPYING-gpl2 and COPYING-gpl3 references correspond to those texts.

Corresponding source is available from the official release URLs:
https://download.gnome.org/sources/gnumeric/1.12/gnumeric-1.12.62.tar.xz
https://download.gnome.org/sources/goffice/0.10/goffice-0.10.62.tar.xz
SOURCE.json records the exact versions and SHA-256 digests. The build fetches
these archives; local verified copies are reusable. The bundled native runtime
archive is retained separately. Product calculation and document code is unchanged.

Building corresponding source

Use Linux x86_64 and the Ubuntu 24.04 base digest in environment/Dockerfile.
The build dependencies are build-essential, bison, flex, gettext, intltool,
pkg-config, libgtk-3-dev, libgsf-1-dev, libxml2-dev, libxslt1-dev, librsvg2-dev,
libbz2-dev, zlib1g-dev, libgsl-dev, itstool and libxml2-utils.

Build GOffice first with:
  ./configure --prefix=/proc/self/fd/9/upstream --with-config-backend=keyfile \
    --disable-introspection --disable-static
  make -j8
  make DESTDIR="$stage" install

Before the Gnumeric build, expose that staged installation with:
  exec 9< "$stage/proc/self/fd/9"
  export PKG_CONFIG_PATH=/proc/self/fd/9/upstream/lib/pkgconfig
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/proc/self/fd/9/upstream/lib

Build Gnumeric with:
  ./configure --prefix=/proc/self/fd/9/upstream --without-python --without-perl \
    --without-gda --disable-introspection --disable-static --disable-component
  make -j8
  make DESTDIR="$stage" install

The installed tree is "$stage/proc/self/fd/9/upstream". Remove headers,
pkg-config files and gtk-doc output for the runtime package; strip native
executables and shared libraries. Package the upstream tree with GNU tar using
--sort=name, --mtime='2024-01-01 00:00:00Z', --owner=0, --group=0 and
--numeric-owner. Compiler and distribution package updates can change the
binary digest; solve.sh verifies the distributed runtime archive before extraction.

The start.sh and CLI wrappers call launch.py, which opens the installation
directory with O_PATH and inherits it as file descriptor 9. This keeps the compiled resource paths valid after an Open
or Save dialog changes the process working directory. The launchers initialize
the upstream time-series function plugin in the keyfile settings backend,
which enables its native Fourier analysis. User-supplied modules are not
loaded. The runtime supplies ordinary GLPK/lp_solve programs for native linear
optimization.

The local confinement.py applies Landlock before product execution; it permits
only the installation, necessary system resources, private state and exchange
directories. Gnumeric additionally permits the GLPK and lp_solve executables
for native optimization. It refuses unconfined startup.

The GUI starts in the document outbox so file dialogs open a readable exchange
directory while the installation root remains non-enumerable.
